    "responsibility": "One complete generated SFUN activation owns actual entry, raw and converted root span, aligned RC census/scan, final frame handoff and physical C exit.",
    "retired": "Per-raw-argument RC allocations, stale post-GC raw C-local reads, separate generated marker lifetime and direct intermediate frame stores; existing generator root prefix and Scheme names retained. No parallel registry or dormant role-record rename.",
    "validation": "Final native C23 rebuild reuses51 generated inputs with no generation. Seven constructor controls;12 histories192 production PBT actions; actual processor1 eight actions; observer mutation shrink13to1; rooted/permanent revoke-GC-drain; closure accessor transfer control. Multi-shot/wide-root consumers,2387 generator checks306 fixtures290 layout assertions15 plans,102 C cases,12 QNT tests,5 disjoint Lean arithmetic theorems and old-module refusal. Original current408-case population completes92.157s:393 pass/15 fail; known-name attribution retained, no whole-family pass.",
    "benefits": "A real before-fix native counterexample distinguishes revoked return permission from physical C quiescence. One lifetime owner retains roots through nested escape/GC; many raw inputs share one allocation and canonical span. Actual census covers the same cells as scanning, preserving multi-shot Scheme control.",
    "costs": "Every RC header+8 bytes; activation+8; GSTATE+40; context unchanged. Raw8 retained header/span/record bytes -256, raw1 +24 before allocator rounding. Final body medians zero -1.325%, one +10.370%, eight -29.618%; no stable universal speedup. Eight-input footprint median+16384 bytes; no peak-memory reduction claim.",
    "process": "One whole19-file post-foundation entry responsibility, not setters or fragments. Live69 paths contain original51 queue plus18 newly dirty paths with one shared Make file; commit leaves prior responsibilities outside. Foundation4/4 and independent SMP1/12 unchanged.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/sfun-entry.org#generated-sfun-activation",
    "models": "Strict OpenSysML SDK binds nine obligations and six actual C refinement maps to shared ASCENT, with missing/stale controls. Existing QNT covers protocol interleavings; Lean proves only array-size/address arithmetic. C source/lock refinement remains conditional cooperative-owner reasoning, not a machine-checked C theorem.",
    "open": "Official15 failures remain and crash-form equivalence is not proved; fresh baseline whole run timed out. General arbitrary foreign-thread admission, asynchronous owner death, ARM C-closure trampoline, code unload, moving-zero timing and stable whole-workflow speedup are outside this complete generated-entry owner. No SMP progress promotion."
